Rule 1 (inputs must not be complex dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 2 (inputs broadcastable per-dimension when ranks match)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 3 (inputs have exactly identical shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 4 (out, if provided, must be a Tensor)
{v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 5 (out shape matches inputs when inputs match exactly)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀ j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, j) = shape(v_2, j) then ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 6 (out dtype matches input and is not complex)
{v_1 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≠ 10
